  pm-gh1597,related,"2026-10-27T03:16:19.265Z","harness:codex","cli:update:dep",detected
  pm-gh1622,related,"2026-10-29T08:53:15.765Z","harness:codex","cli:update:dep",detected
comments[24]:
  - created_at: "2026-10-27T03:16:18.150Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Duplicate check: complete3135-item strict full all-status corpus has no exact GH1609 owner, no unreadable items and no omissions. Request-specific search, open and zero-in-progress inventories were read. Full live pm-02z97f data confirms its earlier audited dead-owner recovery is closed/completed, not newly outstanding. This newly reported crash-inside-fence scenario is a bounded follow-up. Current source includes both owner_dead_recovery_attempt and the independent commit fence in src/core/lock/lock.ts; the report has not yet been independently reproduced. Keep this intake open/unclaimed; do not treat reported symptoms as a proven root cause."
  - created_at: "2026-10-27T04:08:08.403Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Hosted tracker-context-quality correctly identified missing risk/confidence metadata on the new intake. Both fields are supplied through pm (high risk for interrupted-commit safety, low confidence until independent reproduction). Full local tracker-context-quality, graph composition and record integrity now pass their unchanged gates. The item remains open/unclaimed and no reported runtime behavior is claimed fixed."
  - created_at: "2026-10-29T07:37:58.331Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Independent negative control on 2026-10-29: extended the existing real-child SDK recovery integration fixture to terminate the owner while acquireLockLease.fence holds the commit gate. Pre-fix run: acquired-owner and live-owner controls pass, fenced-owner restart fails with lock_conflict (exit 4), 1 failed / 2 passed. Production source gates owner inspection behind a 10-second mtime threshold, longer than the ordinary writer budget. Implementing same-host proven-death gate retirement with retained generation evidence and monotonic duration budgets; preserving live/foreign/legacy owner policy and lease fencing."
  - created_at: "2026-10-29T07:45:21.906Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Focused validation passed all141 tests across7 files, including real killed-owner Node and Bun SDK processes and ordinary CLI restart/history verification. Exact first-rename kill probe (Node builtin rename interception with SIGKILL): published2026.10.21 restart exit0 in0.425s; published2026.10.26 restart exit4 lock_conflict in3.432s; patched checkout restart exit0 in0.428s. Strict history verification passed in all three trackers. Fixtures are outside the repository with isolated local/global PM roots and telemetry disabled. Full coverage/static and hosted verification are next."
  - created_at: "2026-10-29T07:46:29.735Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Isolated baseline negative controls at5f1540b56: Node and Bun fenced-owner restart both fail lock_conflict, and frozen-clock wait exceeds1.5s instead of staying below1s for a100ms budget. The baseline acquired-owner control passes. Same tests on the patched tree passed in the141-test focused run. No test threshold or lease TTL was weakened."
  - created_at: "2026-10-29T07:58:42.264Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Self-review found a further observation race: an observed owner can release its gate before dying, so the path may contain a replacement by the time death is proven. Add a generation re-read after death proof and before retirement. The retained nonempty destination then protects the later interleaving between that re-read and rename. A deterministic fixture now pauses the second recoverer until the replacement owner has published, and separate controls replace or remove the gate before revalidation. Full coverage is running on this revision."
  - created_at: "2026-10-29T08:11:20.133Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "The added replacement-observation negative control fails on PR first head2016f0e68: acquireStaleCleanupGate returns a release function after moving the injected live replacement. Revalidation fix is staged for the next review revision. Evidence also records an explicit two-recoverer schedule where the second rename waits until the first replacement owner has published, exercising the nonempty retained-generation fence rather than relying on scheduler timing."
  - created_at: "2026-10-29T08:15:24.679Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Delivery scope: SDK lock primitives own the recovery and timing semantics; CLI and MCP inherit them without duplicate policy. Public signatures remain unchanged. Gate retirement retains original ownership evidence and rejects live replacements, absent generations, foreign hosts and unverifiable fresh receipts. Lease timestamps and TTL policy remain wall-clock based; only bounded wait durations use the monotonic clock."
  - created_at: "2026-10-29T08:29:50.792Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "First-head PR coverage passed exact 100/100/100/100 and all required runtime, packed-consumer, security and analyzer checks; static failed only on a missing expected_result in new intake pm-gh1622, now corrected. Full local suite retained 2 failures among 11554 tests: missing Homebrew npm module resolution in composed-continuation and one semantic-preview child timeout. Re-running with NODE_PATH from npm root -g and four workers without changing deadlines, membership or coverage thresholds. Added a pre-retirement owner-token recheck after a negative race control proved a live replacement could otherwise be retired."
  - created_at: "2026-10-29T08:47:24.055Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "CodeRabbit review5695009040 identified a pre-existing but reachable cleanup hazard: non-missing owner read errors were treated as ownerless and aged gates removed. Recovery now distinguishes unreadable owners and fails closed; missing/malformed initialization fallback and best-effort release remain unchanged. Added EACCES/EBUSY controls preserving the live receipt through recovery and release, then allowing normal cleanup after the fault clears."
  - created_at: "2026-10-29T08:47:47.252Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Review reference correction: the verified CodeRabbit review is https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1623#pullrequestreview-5694901848; the numeric review reference in the preceding comment was mistyped. Negative control on the pre-fix source fails both EACCES and EBUSY live-owner preservation cases as intended."
  - created_at: "2026-10-29T08:48:52.308Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Review remediation passes all143 focused lock/recovery tests. Before the fix, both injected owner-read failures incorrectly admitted a new holder; after the fix the original gate receipt remains unchanged until readable release succeeds. Static validation passed through tracker context and SDK export parity, then failed the qualified SDK import budget at535ms versus500ms; that original failed attempt is retained and an unchanged-threshold recheck is running."
  - created_at: "2026-10-29T08:53:18.789Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Related release verification intake: the lock-recovery delivery discovered the independently tracked Sentry release blocker. The structured related edge makes that existing narrative reference navigable; it is not a prerequisite for safe lock implementation and does not imply remediation of the upstream package fault."
  - created_at: "2026-10-29T10:05:10.227Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "CodeRabbit current-head review 5695929096 identifies a second competing-recovery path: a valid old generation whose liveness probe is unknown can enter the age fallback without creating the generation tombstone. That permits a dead-owner recoverer paused after its token check to move the age recoverer replacement. Preparing a deterministic mixed-probe negative control and routing readable age-expired generations through the same retained retirement protocol. No source edits will overlap the running coverage process."
  - created_at: "2026-10-29T10:25:02.084Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Review remediation evidence: the deterministic mixed dead-owner/age-based recovery control admitted two holders before the fix and exactly one afterward, retaining the original generation receipt. All readable age-eligible tokens now use the same generation retirement protocol. Complete local coverage on source 943470bca passed 11572 tests with 3 platform skips and exact 100/100/100/100 (zero uncovered counts). The subsequent retirement-path and rollback-assertion delta passes all 166 focused tests across seven files; typecheck, ESLint, docstrings and defect evidence pass. Hosted final-head validation remains required."
  - created_at: "2026-10-29T11:21:03.385Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Final production source 7aef94d8a passes complete local coverage: 11573 tests passed, three platform skips, exact 100/100/100/100 and zero uncovered counts. The bounded mutation gate also passes 345 killed plus seven documented equivalent mutants out of 352, with no unexplained survivor. Required hosted jobs have not yet received runners; Chrome confirms Waiting for a runner to pick up this job. No required check is bypassed."
  - created_at: "2026-10-29T14:09:50.686Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "CodeRabbit review 5698771333 exposes a live-owner retirement race in the inherited one-hour unverified-age fallback: a PID can still be live while missing start identity makes the helper return false. A release and replacement can then occur after token revalidation but before retirement. Reproduce the actual release/replacement interleaving, then reject age alone as proof of death for readable live or unverifiable cleanup owners. Keep normal releases lightweight, preserve positive dead-PID and reusable-PID evidence, and leave lease TTL semantics separate."
    edited_at: "2026-10-29T14:10:44.192Z"
  - created_at: "2026-10-29T14:13:55.548Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "The isolated release/replacement negative control fails on reviewed source 3c5367550: after a still-live legacy owner releases, the paused age recoverer moves its replacement and admits another holder. The repair no longer infers death from age when a readable PID is live but its start identity cannot be verified. The old two-hour legacy assertion is corrected to require preserved ownership; dead PID and verified PID-reuse recovery remain covered. This deliberately tightens the inherited unverified-age policy and avoids retaining coordination artifacts for every normal release."
  - created_at: "2026-10-29T14:22:34.375Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "A second isolated control confirms that an aged foreign-host receipt was incorrectly reclaimed by comparing its PID/start coordinate with this host. Recorded host evidence now must verify before retirement; foreign or unavailable host evidence fails closed. The existing concurrent dead/unknown control now requires the uncertain observer to refuse while the positively dead observer retires the generation. The legacy PID-reuse fixture now uses a valid numeric start coordinate, and unavailable-current-identity coverage exercises a two-hour-old live gate."
  - created_at: "2026-10-29T14:37:57.848Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Review validation: all 151 focused lock, lease, Node/Bun killed-owner, and preflight tests pass. Typecheck, ESLint, docstrings, duplicate detection and packaged documentation links pass. Both the aged-live release/replacement race and aged foreign-host negative controls fail against 3c5367550 and pass with the current policy. Full source coverage is running; it is not yet a passing receipt."
  - created_at: "2026-10-29T15:00:13.498Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Full source verification of05a34455f passes11578 tests with3 platform skips and exact100/100/100/100 (71468 statements,55073 branches,14715 functions,67529 lines). CodeRabbit review5699852471 adds two minor follow-ups: document recovery after a host/boot identity change, and make the local Bun fixture conditional while retaining mandatory CI Bun coverage. Production behavior remains fixed; these follow-ups will change documentation and fixture selection only. Concurrent repository-context-quality passed context/retrieval/token providers but its queued refusal test reached the existing300s process limit; rerun it alone after runners settle, without changing the limit."
  - created_at: "2026-10-29T15:04:36.840Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Review follow-up verification: all4 killed-owner/live-owner integration cases pass with Bun installed. An isolated PATH without Bun passes3 applicable cases locally; the same PATH with CI=1 fails exactly the Bun case with spawn bun ENOENT, proving hosted membership remains mandatory. Typecheck, ESLint and packaged docs links pass. Configuration guidance now explains explicit operator quarantine only after all writers are stopped and original-owner death is independently established, preserving gate bytes and recovery receipts without overriding lease TTL. No production source changed after the11578-test exact-coverage pass."
  - created_at: "2026-10-29T19:40:07.584Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Review4416668051 independently reproduced with EACCES and EBUSY owner-file read faults: both new release regressions fail before the implementation change (13 existing controls pass). The owner now retries at most three inconclusive reads with the existing short jittered delay, then retains ambiguous metadata; a different token is never removed. Actual linked run test-local-mvty638u-mw6emq passes150 tests across7 files, including persistent read failures, token replacements, killed writers, monotonic wait, and Node/Bun public SDK cases. Full exact-head hosted gates remain required before merge."
  - created_at: "2026-10-30T00:57:01.259Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Current full-review suggestion to restore a finite stale-cleanup owner fallback was assessed against the live completed safety contract, documented recovery policy and existing release/replacement race regression. A live PID without start identity cannot prove original-owner death; after a token read, its release can admit a replacement before a pending retirement rename. Age-based retirement reintroduces that race. Retained the existing policy and replied once to the inline finding with the documented exclusive-access recovery procedure; no automatic ownership override or lock-source change was made."
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-29T07:45:23.237Z","harness:codex","Owner-death recovery must cover every coordination layer held by a writer, including the commit gate. A short writer budget cannot recover a gate whose owner is only inspected after a longer age grace. Preserve the retired generation so simultaneous recoverers cannot remove its live replacement, and measure wait deadlines independently of wall-clock lease timestamps."
  "2026-10-29T10:46:55.208Z","harness:codex","A generation-retirement fence is safe only when every eligible removal path for a readable token participates in it. Test mixed liveness outcomes between concurrent recoverers, pause one after its token check until the other publishes a replacement, and prove exactly one holder plus unchanged original recovery evidence. A passing two-dead-owner race alone does not cover the age-policy fallback."
